 "id": "AT-P-13",
 "note": "ROOT-RULINGS R-2/R-5: with no usable perl (a perl on PATH older than 5.28: a stand-in that runs this host's perl with STORE_TEST_PERL_V=5.026003; the launcher checks no version, main.pl's guard runs the launcher's fallback for a hook (the path the launcher's hook wrapper hands it), stdin unread; the stand-in counts its starts, one per hook, and refuses anything else), hook PreCompact prints nothing, exits 0 and appends one helper_runtime_missing row (the launcher's shell fallback: under the default ~/.local/state/<plugin>/handoffs/.watch, STATE-ROOT, or $XDG_STATE_HOME/<plugin>/handoffs/.watch while handoff_root is the default and XDG_STATE_HOME is an absolute path, and nothing under ~/.claude/handoffs); any other subcommand prints REFUSED: helper-runtime and exits 3. 0.1.4 T-15: the fallback writes its row only under an absolute folder that no folder from it up to / holds a .git (folder or file: a git work tree) or a .planning folder, and with no .planning part (also one not made yet, any letter case); the walk runs on the path as given and from its deepest existing folder read through symlinks (cd -P); a root in a git work tree (also through a symlink), a relative root and a .planning root get no row and no folder, the hook still exits 0 with nothing on stdout; a handoff_root or log_dir that is not an absolute path (root-invalid in the helper) gets no row, which would land under the hook's working folder (an exec step sets those roots: the runner's home guard refuses a root env value that is not absolute)",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
